      "message": "David: Do you know if we need the intermediate cast to `uint32_t`?\n\nIn line 43, the expression `(uint64_t)c3 \u003c\u003c 48` does not go through an intermediate cast to `uint16_t`. I assume it is because any extra 1 bits from sign extension of a negative `int16_t` will be shifted out. By analogy, we should not need the intermediate cast to `uint32_t` here either.",
